# Review ownership. GitHub reads the last matching pattern.
#
# `@nonagenticai/maintainers` is the owner of record: the team exists, and the repository owner is
# a maintainer of it. The `main` ruleset keeps `require_code_owner_review: false`, so these
# requests are notifications, never a gate; the owner decision (#93) is a code-owner review on the
# **sensitive paths only**.
#
# The blanket `* @nonagenticai/maintainers` line was removed on 2026-11-17: it requested the team
# on every pull request, including the automated registry refreshes, and nothing could dismiss
# that request — the Actions token cannot resolve an org team node, so the request reached the
# owner's inbox and blocked nothing. Do not re-add `*` while the ruleset leaves code-owner review
# unarmed; arm the ruleset first if a blanket gate is ever wanted.

# Sensitive paths: the CI definitions and the review policy itself.
/.github/workflows/** @nonagenticai/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS @nonagenticai/maintainers
/SECURITY.md @nonagenticai/maintainers
/scripts/ci/** @nonagenticai/maintainers
